# PIXEL_LEVEL_REFERENCE_PARITY

Binding method for all OMA visual / UI / UX parity work against Planable (`DEC-017`). Supersedes auditor text-only or inventory-only visual PASS claims.

## 1. Invalid evidence for visual PASS

A page **cannot** pass from any of:

- CSS token inspection alone
- component inventory alone
- unit tests alone
- route availability alone
- DOM class names alone
- an auditor’s text-only verdict alone

## 2. Required evidence per visible surface

Every visible surface requires:

1. Planable reference screenshot (or `OFFICIAL_DOC_REFERENCE` / `OMA_ADAPTATION` with closest grammar)
2. OMA rejected/before screenshot
3. OMA after screenshot
4. Comparable component crops
5. Measured geometry (JSON)
6. Interaction proof
7. Visual diff / heatmap
8. Final human-readable verdict

## 3. OMA-only functionality

When OMA has no direct Planable screen:

- Map to Planable’s closest component and interaction grammar
- Label `OMA_ADAPTATION`
- Still provide screenshots and measurements

## 4. Owner review gate

**No visual status may become PASS while Owner review is rejected.**

Allowed labels while Owner has rejected: `NOT_PASS`, `REVOKED_BY_OWNER`, `READY_FOR_OWNER_REVIEW`, `PENDING_OWNER`, `REJECTED`.

## 5. Screenshot validity

Screenshot evidence must use:

- production Web build (`next start`, not `next dev`)
- loaded fonts (`document.fonts.ready`)
- stable seeded data
- completed relevant network requests
- settled animations
- exact target viewport
- zoom 100%, consistent device scale
- no DevTools / terminal overlay on the capture viewport
- no development badge

## 6. Invalid screenshots

Screenshots from any of the following are **invalid**:

- `next dev`
- loading / skeleton frames
- broken assets
- unstable animation frames

## 7. Capture roots (gitignored raw media)

- OMA rejected: `artifacts/oma-planable-pixel-parity/oma-rejected/`
- Planable reference: `artifacts/oma-planable-pixel-parity/planable-reference/`
- OMA after + diffs: `artifacts/oma-planable-pixel-parity/`
- Scrubbed metadata: `.reference/009-planable-pixel-parity/`

Filenames must include evidence ID, route, view, state, locale, viewport, SHA.

## 8. Geometry / pixel targets (LIVE_VERIFIED)

Comparable component targets after content-only normalization:

- geometry / spacing delta ≤ 2px
- radius exact where LIVE_VERIFIED
- control height exact
- reference colors exact
- typography size / line-height exact
- chrome pixel mismatch ≤ 3%

A numeric threshold alone does **not** override an obvious visible defect.
